  5551:           should be used to prevent unexpected removal of the device or media.
  5552: 
  5553:                                                                                                                                               89
  5554: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  5555: 
  5556:                                                       Annex D.
  5557: 
  5558:                                                                 (informative)
  5559: 
  5560:                           Identify device data for ATA devices below 8 GB
  5561: 
  5562: D.1 Definitions and background information
  5563: 
  5564: The following abbreviations are used in this annex:
  5565: - 528 MB is used to describe a drive that has 1,032,192 sectors or 528,482,304 bytes.
  5566: - 8 GB is used to describe a drive that has 16,515,072 sectors or 8,455,716,864 bytes.
  5567: The original IBM PC BIOS (Basic Input/Output System) imposed several restrictions on the support of disk
  5568: drives, and these have been incorporated into many higher level software products. One such restriction
  5569: limits the capacity of a hard disk drive. Most BIOS software cannot support a disk drive with more than
  5570: 1,024 cylinders, 16 heads and 63 sectors per track. The maximum addressable capacity of an ATA disk
  5571: drive under this scheme is 528 MB.
  5572: There is growing support of auto-configuration for disk drives on PC systems. The auto-configuration
  5573: capability usually resides in the BIOS and uses the Identify Drive command data to configure an ATA disk
  5574: drive.
  5575: This annex defines rules for the Identify Drive data of all capacity ATA disk drives and allows BIOS support
  5576: of ATA drives up to 8 GB using Cylinder/Head/Sector (CHS) addressing.
  5577: This specification defines information that newer BIOSs and system software can use to determine the true
  5578: size of a disk drive and access the full capacity of the drive.
  5579: 
  5580: D.2 Cylinder, head and sector addressing
  5581: 
  5582: BIOSs and other software that operate an ATA disk drive in CHS (Cylinder, Head and Sector) addressing
  5583: mode use Identify Drive data words 1, 3, 6 and words 53-58 to ascertain the appropriate translation mode to
  5584: use and determine the capacity of an ATA disk drive.
  5585: Maximum compatibility is achieved if the following rules are obeyed. These rules limit the values placed into
  5586: words 1, 3, 6, and 53-58. The rules specified here for CHS addressing apply to drives up to 8 GB.
  5587: 
  5588: D.2.1 Word 1
  5589: 
  5590: For drives less than or equal to 528 MB, Identify Data word 1 (Default Cylinders) shall not specify a value
  5591: greater than 1,024.
  5592: If a drive is greater than 528 MB but less than or equal to 8 GB, the maximum value that shall be placed into
  5593: this word is determined by the value in Word 3 as shown in the following table.
  5594: 
  5595: 90
  5596:                                                                                         X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  5597: 
  5598:                                               Value in Word 3  Maximum value in Word 1
  5599:                                                      1 1h      65,535 FFFFh
  5600:                                                      2 2h      65,535 FFFFh
  5601:                                                      3 3h      65,535 FFFFh
  5602:                                                      4 4h      65,535 FFFFh
  5603:                                                      5 5h      32,767 7FFFh
  5604:                                                      6 6h      32,767 7FFFh
  5605:                                                      7 7h      32,767 7FFFh
  5606:                                                      8 8h      32,767 7FFFh
  5607:                                                      9 9h      16,383 3FFFh
  5608:                                                                16,383 3FFFh
  5609:                                                    10 Ah       16,383 3FFFh
  5610:                                                    11 Bh       16,383 3FFFh
  5611:                                                    12 Ch       16,383 3FFFh
  5612:                                                    13 Dh       16,383 3FFFh
  5613:                                                    14 Eh       16,383 3FFFh
  5614:                                                    15 Fh       16,383 3FFFh
  5615:                                                    16 10h
  5616: 
  5617: The value in this word shall not change.
  5618: 
  5619: D.2.2 Word 3
  5620: 
  5621: Identify Data word 3 (Default Heads) shall not specify a value greater than 16.
  5622: The value in this word shall not change.
  5623: 
  5624: D.2.3 Word 6
  5625: 
  5626: For drives of 8 GB or less, Identify Data word 6 (Default Sectors) shall not specify a value greater than 63.
  5627: The value in this word shall not change.
  5628: 
  5629: D.2.4 Use of words 53 through 58
  5630: 
  5631: ATA drives that are over 528 MB shall implement words 53-58. Drives not over 528 MB may also implement
  5632: these words. These words define the addressing for all sectors accessible in CHS mode.
  5633: 
  5634: D.2.5 Word 53
  5635: 
  5636: Identify Data word 53 bit 0 shall be set to 1 at all times that the drive is in a valid translation mode. Some
  5637: drives may have translation modes that cannot be supported. An attempt to put a drive into one of these
  5638: unsupported modes shall cause word 53 bit 0 to be set to 0 with words 54-58 cleared to zero until a valid
  5639: translation mode is established.
  5640: 
  5641: D.2.6 Word 54
  5642: 
  5643: Identify Data word 54 (Current Cylinders) shall specify the number of full logical cylinders that can be
  5644: accessed in the current translation mode. If an Initialize Drive Parameters command has not been executed,
  5645: the contents of this word shall be the same as word 1. If an Initialize Drive Parameters command has been
  5646: executed, this word is the integer result of dividing the total number of user sectors (this value may be in
  5647: words 60-61) by the number of sectors per logical cylinder ( [word55] x [word56] ), but shall not be a value
  5648: greater than 65,535.
  5649: 
  5650:                                                                                                                91
  5651: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  5652: 
  5653: D.2.7 Word 55
  5654: 
  5655: Identify Data word 55 (Current Heads) is the number of heads specified by the last Initialize Drive
  5656: Parameters command. This word may contain a value of between 1 and 16. If an Initialize Drive
  5657: Parameters command has not been executed, the contents of this word shall be the same as word 3.
  5658: 
  5659: D.2.8 Word 56
  5660: 
  5661: Identify Data word 56 (Current Sectors) is the number of sectors specified by the last Initialize Drive
  5662: Parameters command. This word may contain a value of between 1 and 255. If an Initialize Drive
  5663: Parameters command has not been executed, the contents of this word shall be the same as word 6.
  5664: 
  5665: D.2.9 Words 57-58
  5666: 
  5667: Identify Data words 57-58 contain a 32-bit value that shall be equal to [word54] multi [word55] multi [word56].
  5668: If words 60-61, LBA sectors, are not zero, words 57-58 shall be less than or equal to the value in words 60-61
  5669: at all times.
  5670: D.3 Logical block addressing
  5671: It is recommended that ATA drives over 528 MB support Logical Block Addressing (LBA).
  5672: 
  5673: D.3.11 Words 60-61
  5674: 
  5675: Identify Data words 60-61 shall specify the total number of user sectors available in LBA mode at all times.
  5676: This value shall be equal to or greater than the value in words 57-58 at all times. The contents of these
  5677: words shall not change.
  5678: 
  5679: D.3.2 Orphan Sectors
  5680: 
  5681: The sectors, if any, between the last sector addressable in CHS mode and the last sector addressable in LBA
  5682: mode are known as "orphan" sectors. A drive may or may not allow access to these sectors in CHS
  5683: addressing mode.
  5684: The values in words 1, 3, and 6 should be selected such that the number of orphan sectors is minimized.
  5685: Normally, the number of orphan sectors should not exceed ( [word55] multi [word56] - 1 ). However, the host
  5686: system can create conditions where there are a larger number of orphans sectors by issuing the Initialize
  5687: Drive Parameters command with values other than the values in words 3 and 6.
  5688: 
