  2467: 7.13 EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC
  2468: 
  2469: OPCODE - 90h
  2470: TYPE - Mandatory.
  2471: PROTOCOL - Non-data.
  2472: INPUTS - None, except that the device selection bit in the Device/Head register is ignored.
  2473: NORMAL OUTPUTS - The diagnostic code written into the Error register is an 8-bit code as shown in table
  2474: 11, and not as defined in 6.2.8.
  2475: 
  2476:                                                                                                                                               33
  2477: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  2478: 
  2479:           Code            Table 11 - Diagnostic Codes
  2480:     01h
  2481:     00h, 02h-7Fh                                  Description
  2482:     81h                  Device 0 passed, Device 1 passed or not present
  2483:     80h, 82h-FFh         Device 0 failed, Device 1 passed or not present
  2484:                          Device 1 failed, Device 0 passed
  2485:                          Device 1 failed, Device 0 failed
  2486: 
  2487: The meaning of values other than 01h and 81h are vendor specific and should be considered a diagnostic
  2488: failed condition.
  2489: 
  2490: ERROR OUTPUTS - None. All error information is returned as a diagnostic code in the Error register.
  2491: 
  2492: PREREQUISITES - None.
  2493: 
  2494: DESCRIPTION - This command shall perform the internal diagnostic tests implemented by the device. See
  2495: also 6.2.8 and 6.2.12. The DEV bit in the Drive/Head register is ignored. Both devices, if present, shall
  2496: execute this command.
  2497: 
  2498: Device 0 performs the following operations for this command:
  2499:           a) Device 0 sets the BSY bit within 400 ns after the EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command is
  2500:           received;
  2501:           b) Device 0 performs diagnostics;
  2502:           c) Device 0 resets the Command Block registers to the following:
  2503:                      Cylinder Low = 00h Cylinder HigH = 00h
  2504:                      Sector Count = 01h Device/Head = 00h
  2505:                      Sector Number = 01h
  2506:           d) Device 0 posts diagnostic results to bits 6-0 of the Error Register;
  2507:           e) If Device 0 detected that Device 1 is present during the most recent power on or hardware reset
  2508:           sequence, then Device 0 waits up to 6 seconds from the time that the EXECUTE DEVICE
  2509:           DIAGNOSTIC command was received for Device 1 to assert PDIAG-. If PDIAG- is asserted within 6
  2510:           seconds, Device 0 sets bit 7 to zero in the Error Register, else Device 0 sets bit 7 equal to 1 in the
  2511:           Error Register;
  2512:           If device 1 was not detected during the most recent power up or hardware reset sequence, then
  2513:           Device 0 sets bit 7 to zero in the Error register;
  2514:           f) Device 0 clears the BSY bit when ready to accept commands that do not require the DRDY bit to
  2515:           be equal to 1;
  2516: 
  2517:      NOTE 17 - Device 0 shall clear the BSY bit within 6 seconds from the time that the EXECUTE
  2518:      DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command was received.
  2519: 
  2520:           g) Device 0 sets the DRDY bit when ready to accept any command.
  2521:      NOTE 18 - Steps f) and g) may occur at the same time. While no maximum time is specified for the
  2522:      DRDY bit to be set to one to occur, a host is advised to allow up to 2 minutes for the DRDY bit to be
  2523:      set to one. See Figure 7.
  2524: 
  2525: Device 1 performs the following operations for this command:
  2526:           a) Device 1 sets the BSY bit within 400 ns after the EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command is
  2527:           received;
  2528:           b) Device 1 negates PDIAG- within 1 ms after the command is received;
  2529:           c) Device 1 performs diagnostics;
  2530:           d) Device 1 resets the Command Block registers to the following:
  2531:                      Cylinder Low = 00h Cylinder HigH = 00h
  2532:                      Sector Count = 01h Device/Head = 00h
  2533:                      Sector Number = 01h
  2534:           e) Device 1 sets bit 7 of the Error register to zero and posts its diagnostic results to bits 6 through 0
  2535:           of Error register;
  2536: 
  2537: 34
  2538:                                                                       X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  2539: 
  2540:      f) Device 1 clears the BSY bit when ready to accept commands that do not require the DRDY bit to
  2541:      be equal to one;
  2542:      g) If Device 1 passed its diagnostics without error in step c), Device 1 asserts PDIAG-. If the
  2543:      diagnostics failed, Device 1 does not assert PDIAG- and continues to the next step;
  2544:      NOTE 19 - Device 1 shall clear the BSY bit and assert PDIAG- within 5 seconds of the time that the
  2545:      EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command is received.
  2546:      h) Device 1 sets the DRDY bit when ready to accept any command.
  2547: NOTE 20 - Steps f), g) and h) may occur at the same time. While no maximum time is specified
  2548: for the DRDY bit to set to one, a host is advised to allow up to 2 minutes for the DRDY bit to be
  2549: equal to one. See figure 7.
  2550: 
