  1668: 6.2.9 Features register
  1741:           The BSY bit shall be set by the device under the following circumstances:
  1742: 
  1743:                 a) within 400 ns after either the negation of RESET- or the setting of the SRST bit in the Device
  1744:                 Control register;
  1745:                 b) within 400 ns after the acceptance of a command if the DRQ bit is not set;
  1746:                 c) between blocks of a data transfer during PIO data in commands if the DRQ bit is not set;
  1747:                 d) after the transfer of a data block during PIO data out commands if the DRQ bit is not set;
  1748:                 e) during the data transfer of DMA commands if the DRQ bit is not set.
  1749: 
  1750:           The device shall not set the BSY bit at any other time.
  1751:           When the BSY bit is set due to the negation of RESET- or the setting of the SRST bit, the BSY bit
  1752:           shall remain set until the device has completed processing of the reset condition.
  1753:           When a command is accepted either the BSY bit shall be set, or if the BSY bit is cleared, the DRQ
  1754:           bit shall be set, until command completion.
  1755:      NOTE 14 - There may be times when the BSY bit is set and then cleared so quickly, that the host
  1756:      may not be able to detect that the BSY bit had been set.
  1757: 
  1758: � DRDY (Device Ready) is set to indicate that the device is capable of accepting all command codes. This
  1759:      bit shall be cleared at power on. Devices that implement the power management features shall maintain
  1760:      the DRDY bit equal to one when they are in the Idle or Standby power modes. When the state of the
  1761:      DRDY bit changes, it shall not change again until after the host reads the Status register.
  1762:           When the DRDY bit is equal to zero, a device responds as follows:
  1763:                 a) the device shall accept and attempt to execute the EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC and
  1764:                 INITIALIZE DEVICE PARAMETERS commands;
  1765:                 b) the device should reject all other commands codes by setting the ABRT bit in the Error
  1766:                 register and setting the ERR bit in the Status register before clearing the BSY bit to signal the
  1767:                 command completion. If a device accepts commands other than EXECUTE DEVICE
  1768:                 DIAGNOSTIC and INITIALIZE DEVICE PARAMETERS during the time the DRDY bit is equal to
  1769:                 zero, the results are vendor specific.
  1770: 
  1771: 20
  1772:                                                                                                                X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  1773: 
  1774: � DF (Device Fault) indicates a device fault error has been detected. The internal status or internal
  1775:      conditions that causes this error to be indicated is vendor specific.
  1776: 
  1777: � DSC (Device Seek Complete) indicates that the device heads are settled over a track. When an error
  1778:      occurs, this bit shall not be changed until the Status Register is read by the host, at which time the bit
  1779:      again indicates the current Seek Complete status.
  1780: 
  1781: � DRQ (Data Request) indicates that the device is ready to transfer a word or byte of data between the
  1782:      host and the device.
  1783: 
  1784: � CORR (Corrected Data) is used to indicate a correctable data error. The definition of what constitutes a
  1785:      correctable error is vendor specific. This condition does not terminate a data transfer.
  1786: 
  1787: � IDX (Index) is vendor specific.
  1788: � ERR (Error) indicates that an error occurred during execution of the previous command. The bits in the
  1789: 
  1790:      Error register have additional information regarding the cause of the error. Once the device has set the
  1791:      error bit, the device shall not change the contents of the following items until a new command has been
  1792:      accepted, the SRST bit is set to one or RESET- is asserted:
  1793: 
  1794:                      the ERR bit in the status register
  1795:                      Error register
  1796:                      Cylinder High register
  1797:                      Cylinder Low register
  1798:                      Sector Count register
  1799:                      Sector Number register
  1800:                      Device/Head register.
