  1802: 7. General operational requirements
  1803: 
  1804: 7.1 Reset response
  1805: 
  1806: There are three types of reset in ATA. The following is a suggested method of classifying reset actions:
  1807: 
  1808: � Power On Reset: the device executes a series of electrical circuitry diagnostics, spins up the HDA, tests
  1809:      speed and other mechanical parametrics, and sets default values.
  1810: 
  2573: NORMAL OUTPUTS - Vendor specific.
  2574: ERROR OUTPUTS - Aborted Command if the device does not support this command. All other errors are
