  2580: 7.15 IDENTIFY DEVICE
  2581: 
  2582: OPCODE - ECh
  2583: TYPE - Mandatory
  2584: PROTOCOL - PIO data in.
  2585: INPUTS - None.
  2586: NORMAL OUTPUTS - None required.
  2587: ERROR OUTPUTS - None.
  2588: PREREQUISITES - None.
  2589: 
  2590:                                                                       35
  2591: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  2592: 
  2593: DESCRIPTION - The IDENTIFY DEVICE command enables the host to receive parameter information from
  2594: the device.
  2595: Some devices may have to read the media in order to complete this command.
  2596: When the command is issued, the device sets the BSY bit, prepares to transfer the 256 words of device
  2597: identification data to the host, sets the DRQ bit, clears the BSY bit, and generates an interrupt. The host can
  2598: then transfer the data by reading the Data register. The parameter words in the buffer have the arrangement
  2599: and meanings defined in Table 12. All reserved bits or words shall be zero.
  2600: The F/V column indicates if the word or part of a word has fixed (F) contents that do not change, variable (V)
  2601: contents that may change depending on the device state or the commands executed by the device, X for
  2602: words with vendor specific data which may be fixed or variable, and R for reserved words which shall be
  2603: zero. For removable media devices, the value of fields indicated as fixed (F) may change when media is
  2604: removed or changed.
  2605: Some parameters are defined as a group of bits. A word which is defined as a set of bits is transmitted with
  2606: indicated bits on the respective data bus bit (e.g., bit 15 appears on DD15).
  2607: Some parameters are defined as a sixteen bit value. A word which is defined as a sixteen bit value places
  2608: the most significant bit of the value on bit DD15 and the least significant bit on bit DD0.
  2609: Some parameters are defined as 32 bit values (e.g., words 57 and 58). Such fields are transferred using two
  2610: word transfers. The device shall first transfer the least significant bits, bits 15 through 0 of the value, on bits
  2611: DD15 through DD0 respectively. After the least significant bits have been transferred, the most significant
  2612: bits, bits 31 through 16 of the value, shall be transferred on DD15 through DD0 respectively.
  2613: Some parameters are defined as a string of ASCII characters. For the string "Copyright", the character `C' is
  2614: the first byte, `o' is the 2nd byte, etc. When such fields are transferred, the order of transmission is:
  2615: 
  2616:  the 1st character (`C') is on bits DD15 through DD8 of the first word
  2617:  the 2nd character (`o') is on bits DD7 through DD0 of the first word
  2618:  the 3rd character (`p') is on bits DD15 through DD8 of the second word
  2619:  the 4th character (`y') is on bits DD7 through DD0 of the second word
  2620:  etc.
  2621: 
  2622: 36
  2623:                                                                 X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
