  2817: The number of user-addressable logical heads per logical cylinder in the default translation mode.
  2818: 7.15.5 Word 4: Vendor specific data.
  2819: 7.15.6 Word 5: Vendor specific data.
  2820: 7.15.7 Word 6: Number of logical sectors per logical track
  2821: The number of user-addressable logical sectors per logical track in the default translation mode.
  2822: 7.15.8 Words 7-9: Vendor specific data.
  2823: 7.15.9 Words 10-19: Serial Number
  2824: If word 10 of this field is 0000h, then the serial number is not specified and the definition of the remaining
  2891: 7.15.20 Word 52: Single Word DMA data transfer cycle timing mode
  2892: 
  2893: The DMA transfer timing for each ATA device falls into categories which have unique parametric timing
  2894: specifications. To determine the proper device timing category, compare the Cycle Time specified in figure
  2895: 11 with the contents of this field. The value returned in Bits 15-8 should fall into one of the categories
  2896: specified in figure 11 (i.e. 0, 1, or 2), and if it does not, then Mode 0 shall be used to serve as the default
  2897: timing.
  2898: The contents of this word shall be ignored if Words 62 or 63 are supported.
  2899: 
  2900: 7.15.21 Word 53: Field Validity
  2901: 
  2902: If bit 0 of word 53 is set, then the values reported in words 54 through 58 are valid. If this bit is cleared, the
  2903: values reported in words 54 through 58 may be valid. If bit 1 of word 53 is set, then the values reported in
  2904: words 64 through 70 are valid. If this bit is cleared, the values reported in words 64-70 are not valid. Any
  2905: device which supports PIO Mode 3 or above, or supports Multiword DMA Mode 1 or above, shall set bit 1 of
  2906: word 53 and support the fields contained in words 64 through 70.
  2907: 
  2908: 7.15.22 Word 54: Number of current logical cylinders
  2909: 
  2910: The number of user-addressable logical cylinders in the current translation mode.
  2911:      NOTE 22 - For ATA-1 devices, if the INITIALIZE DEVICE PARAMETERS command has not been
  2912:      issued to the device then the value of this word is vendor specific.
  2913: 
  2914: 7.15.23 Word 55: Number of current logical heads
  2915: 
  2916: The number of user-addressable logical heads per logical cylinder in the current translation mode.
  2917:      NOTE 23 - For ATA-1 devices, if the INITIALIZE DEVICE PARAMETERS command has not been
  2918:      issued to the device then the value of this word is vendor specific.
  2919: 
  2920: 7.15.24 Word 56: Number of current logical sectors per logical track
  2921: 
  2922: The number of user-addressable logical sectors per logical track in the current translation mode.
  2923:      NOTE 24 - For ATA-1 devices, if the INITIALIZE DEVICE PARAMETERS command has not been
  2924:      issued to the device then the value of this word is vendor specific.
  2925: 
  2926: 7.15.25 Word 57-58: Current capacity in sectors
  2927: 
  2928: The current capacity in sectors excludes all sectors used for device-specific purposes. The value reported in
  2929: this field shall be the product of words 54, 55 and 56.
  2930: 
  2931: 7.15.26 Word 59: Multiple sector setting
  2932: 
  2933: If bit 8 is set, then bits 7-0 reflect the number of sectors currently set to transfer on a READ/WRITE
  2934: MULTIPLE command. If word 47 bits 7-0 are zero then word 59 bits 8-0 shall also be zero.
  2935: 
  2936: 7.15.27 Word 60-61: Total number of user addressable sectors
