  3100: 
  3101:           NOTE 26 - Previous ATA specifications were unclear about the error conditions that this command
  3102:           may indicate. Some implementations do not indicate any errors for this command even when the
  3103:           command fails. However, most of these implementations do fail media access commands if a valid
  3104:           CHS translation is not in effect.
  3105: PREREQUISITES - None.
  3106: DESCRIPTION - This command enables the host to set the number of logical sectors per track and the
  3107: number of logical heads minus 1, per logical cylinder for the current CHS translation mode.
  3108: Upon receipt of the command, the device sets the BSY bit, saves the parameters, clears the BSY bit, and
  3109: generates an interrupt.
  3110: A device shall support the CHS translation described in words 1, 3 and 6 of the IDENTIFY DEVICE
  3111: information. Support of other CHS translations is optional.
  3112: If the requested CHS translation is not supported, the device shall set the Error bit in the Status register and
  3113: set the Aborted Command bit in the Error register before clearing the BSY bit in the Status register.
  3114: If the requested CHS translation is not supported, the device shall fail all media access commands with an ID
  3115: Not Found error until a valid CHS translation is established.
  3116:           NOTE 27 - Host implementations should use the default CHS translation mode described in words 1,
  3117:           3 and 6 of the IDENTIFY DEVICE information. Future ATA specifications may restrict the valid input
  3118:           parameters for this command to these values.
  3119:           NOTE 28 - Some ATA-1 devices require that this command be issued prior to media access.
