  3138: 
  3139: OPCODE - 00h
  3140: TYPE - Optional.
  3141: PROTOCOL - Non-data.
  3142: INPUTS - None required.
  3143: NORMAL OUTPUTS - The Command Block registers, other than the Error and Status registers, are not
  3144: changed by this command.
  3145: ERROR OUTPUTS - This command always fails with an Aborted Command error.
  3146: PREREQUISITES - None.
  3147: DESCRIPTION - This command enables a host which can only perform 16-bit register accesses, to check
  3148: device status. The device shall respond, as it does to an unrecognized command, by setting Aborted
  3149: Command in the Error register, Error in the Status register, clearing Busy in the Status register, and asserting
  3150: INTRQ.
  3151: 
  3152:      NOTE 29 - When a 16-bit host writes to the Device/Head Register, one byte contains the Command
  3153:      register, so the device sees a new command when the intended purpose is only to select a device.
  3154: 
  3155: Both devices may be Busy but not necessarily Ready, e.g.; Device 0 may be ready, but not device 1. To
  3156: check this possibility a typical sequence for an 8-bit host would be:
  3157: 
  3158:        a) Read the Status register (wait until Busy False);
  3159:        b) Select the device (write to the Device/Head Register);
  3160:        c) Read the Status register (wait until Busy False and Ready True);
  3161:        d) Send the command (write to the Command register).
  3162: 
  3163: 46
  3164:                                                                       X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  3165: 
  3166: As a 16-bit host executes b and d simultaneously, a problem occurs if the device being selected is Not
  3167: Ready at the time the command is issued.
  3168: 
