  4945: 
  4946:                                                                                  77
  4947: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  4948: 
  4949:                                                 Annex A.
  4950: 
  4951:                                                         (informative)
  4952: 
  4953:     Diagnostic and reset considerations from a device firmware standpoint
  4954: 
  4955: A.1 Power on and hardware reset (RESET-)
  4956: 
  4957: DASP- is read by Device 0 to determine if Device 1 is present. If Device 1 is present Device 0 shall read
  4958: PDIAG- to determine when it is valid to clear the BSY bit and whether Device 1 has powered on or reset
  4959: without error, otherwise Device 0 clears the BSY bit whenever it is ready to accept commands. Device 0
  4960: may assert DASP- to indicate device activity.
  4961: 
  4962: A.2 Software reset
  4963: 
  4964: If Device 1 is present Device 0 shall read PDIAG- to determine when it is valid to clear the BSY bit and
  4965: whether Device 1 has reset without any errors, otherwise Device 0 shall simply reset and clear the BSY bit.
  4966: DASP- is asserted by Device 0 (and Device 1 if it is present) in order to indicate device active.
  4967: 
  4968: A.3 Device diagnostic command
  4969: 
  4970: If Device 1 is present, Device 0 shall read PDIAG- to determine when it is valid to clear the BSY bit and if
  4971: Device 1 passed or failed the EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command, otherwise Device 0 shall simply
  4972: execute its diagnostics and then clear the BSY bit. DASP- is asserted by Device 0 (and Device 1 if it is
  4973: present) in order to indicate the device is active.
  4974: 
  4975: A.4 Truth table
  4976: 
  4977: In all the above cases: Power on, RESET-, software reset, and the EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC
  4978: command the Device 0 Error register is calculated as shown in the following table:
  4979: 
  4980:     Device 1 present?    PDIAG- asserted?  Device 0 passed  Error register
  4981:              Yes                  Yes              Yes            01h
  4982:              Yes                  Yes               No            0xh
  4983:              Yes                   No              Yes            81h
  4984:              Yes                   No               No            8xh
  4985:               No                                   Yes            01h
  4986:               No              (not read)            No            0xh
  4987:                               (not read)
  4988: 
  4989: Where x indicates the appropriate Diagnostic Code for the Power on, RESET-, software reset, or device
  4990: diagnostics error.
  4991: 
