 succeeded in 188ms:
  3821: BSY bit is changed from 1 to 0 during command execution.
  3822: 
  3823: A command shall only be interrupted with a hardware or software reset. The result of writing to the
  3824: Command register while the BSY bit is equal to one or the DRQ bit is equal to one is unpredictable and may
  3825: result in data corruption. A command should only be interrupted by a reset at times when the host thinks
  3826: there may be a problem, such as a device that is no longer responding. Host programmers are warned
  3827: 
  3828:                                                                                                                                               59
  3829: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  3830: 
  3831: against setting unrealistically short command timeout periods since this may impact a device's ability to
  3832: perform device level retry and data recovery activities.
  3833: 
  3834: 8.1 Power on and hardware resets
  3835: 
  3836: This clause describes the algorithm and timing relationships for Devices 0 and 1 during the processing of
  3837: power on and hardware resets.
  3838: 
  3839: The timing assumes the following:
  3840: 
  3841: a) DASP- is asserted by Device 1 and received by Device 0 at power-on or hardware reset to indicate the
  3842:      presence of Device 1. At all other times it is asserted by Device 0 or Device 1 to indicate when a device
  3843:      is active;
  3844: 
  3845: b) PDIAG- is asserted by Device 1 and detected by Device 0. It is used by Device 1 to indicate to Device 0
  3846:      that it has completed diagnostics without error and is ready to accept commands from the Host (BSY bit
  3847:      is cleared). This does not indicate that the device is ready, only that it can accept commands.
  3848: 
  3849: 8.1.1 Power on and hardware resets - device 0
  3850: 
  3851: a) Host asserts RESET- for a minimum of 25 usec;
  3852: b) Device 0 sets the BSY bit no later than 400 ns after RESET- is negated;
  3853: c) Device 0 negates DASP- no later than 1 ms after RESET- is negated;
  3854: d) Device 0 samples for at least 450 ms for DASP- to be asserted from Device 1. This sampling starts 1 ms
  3855: 
  3856:      after RESET- is negated;
  3857: e) Device 0 performs hardware initialization and diagnostics;
  3858: f) Device 0 may revert to its default condition;
  3859: g) If Device 0 detected that DASP- was asserted during step d), then Device 0 waits up to 31 seconds for
  3860: 
  3861:      Device 1 to assert PDIAG-. If PDIAG- is asserted within 31 seconds, Device 0 sets bit 7 equal to 0 in the
  3862:      Error Register, else Device 0 sets bit 7 equal to 1 in the Error Register. If DASP- assertion was not
  3863:      detected in step d) Device 0 sets bit 7 equal to 0 in the Error Register. In either case the device shall set
  3864:      the Sector Count register to 01h, the Sector Number register to 01h, the Cylinder Low register to 00h, the
  3865:      Cylinder High register to 00h, and the Device/Head register to 00h. Device 0 shall store whether or not
  3866:      Device 1 was detected in step d) because this information is need in order to process any Software reset
  3867:      or EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command later;
  3868: h) Device 0 posts diagnostic results to bits 6-0 of the Error Register;
  3869: i) Device 0 clears the BSY bit when ready to accept commands that do not require the DRDY bit to be equal
  3870:      to 1. Device 0 shall clear the BSY bit no later than 31 seconds from the time that RESET- is negated;
  3871: j) Device 0 sets the DRDY bit when ready to accept any command.
  3872: 
  3873:      NOTE 34 - Steps i) and j) may occur at the same time. While no maximum time is specified for the
  3874:      DRDY bit to be set to 1, a host should allow up to 2 minutes for the DRDY bit to become 1. See
  3875:      figure 8.
  3876: 
  3877: 8.1.2 Power on and hardware resets - device 1
  3878: 
  3879: a) Host asserts RESET- for a minimum of 25 us;
  3880: b) Device 1 sets the BSY bit no later than 400 ns after RESET- is negated;
  3881: c) Device 1 negates DASP- no later than 1 ms after RESET- is negated;
  3882: d) Device 1 negates PDIAG- before asserting DASP-;
  3883: e) Device 1 asserts DASP- no later than 400 ms after RESET- is negated;
  3884: f) Device 1 performs hardware initialization and diagnostics;
  3885: g) Device 1 may revert to its default condition;
  3886: h) Device 1 posts diagnostic results to the Error Register;
  3887: 
  3888: 60
  3889:                                                          X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  3890: 
  3891: i) Device 1 clears the BSY bit when ready to accept commands that do not require the DRDY bit to be equal
  3892:      to 1;
  3893: 
  3894: j) If Device 1 passed its diagnostics without error in step f), Device 1 asserts PDIAG-. If the diagnostics
  3895:      failed, Device 1 does not assert PDIAG- and continues to the next step. Device 1 shall clear the BSY bit,
  3896:      and optionally assert PDIAG-, no later than 30 seconds from the time RESET- is negated. The device
  3897:      shall set the Sector Count register to 01h, the Sector Number register to 01h, the Cylinder Low register to
  3898:      00h, the Cylinder High register to 00h, and the Device/Head register to 00h;
  3899: 
  3900: k) Device 1 sets the DRDY bit when ready to accept any command;
  3901: 
  3902:           NOTE 35 - Steps i), j) and k) may occur at the same time. While no maximum time is specified for
  3903:                 the DRDY bit to be set to 1, a host should allow up to 2 minutes for the DRDY bit to become 1.
  3904:                 See figure 8.
  3905: 
  3906: l) Device 1 negates DASP- after the first command is received or negates DASP- if no command is received
  3907:      within 31 seconds after RESET- is asserted.
  3908: 
