  3933: 8.2 Software reset
  3934: 
  3935: This clause describes the algorithm and timing relationships for Devices 0 and 1 during the processing of
  3936: software resets.
  3937: 
  3938: 8.2.1 Software reset - device 0
  3939: 
  3940: a) Host sets the SRST bit to 1 in the Device Control register;
  3941: b) Device 0 sets BSY bit no later than 400 ns after detecting that the SRST bit is equal to 1;
  3942: c) Device 0 performs hardware initialization and diagnostics;
  3943: d) Device 0 may revert to its default condition;
  3944: e) Device 0 posts diagnostic results to the Error Register;
  3945: f) Device 0 waits for the host to set the SRST bit to 0;
  3946: g) If Device 0 detected that Device 1 is present during the most recent power on or hardware reset sequence,
  3947: 
  3948:      then Device 0 waits up to 31 seconds from the time that the SRST bit to become 0 for Device 1 to assert
  3949:      PDIAG-. If PDIAG- is asserted within 31 seconds, Device 0 sets bit 7 equal to 0 in the Error Register,
  3950:      else Device 0 sets bit 7 equal to 1 in the Error Register. If device 1 was not detected during the most
  3951:      recent power up or hardware reset sequence, then Device 0 sets bit 7 equal to 0 in the Error register. In
  3952:      either case the device shall set the Sector Count register to 01h, the Sector Number register to 01h, the
  3953:      Cylinder Low register to 00h, the Cylinder High register to 00h, and the Device/Head register to 00h;
  3954: h) Device 0 clears the BSY bit when ready to accept commands that do not require the DRDY bit to be equal
  3955:      to 1. Device 0 shall clear the BSY bit no later than 31 seconds from the time that the host sets the SRST
  3956:      bit equal to 0;
  3957: 
  3958:      NOTE 36 - Steps g) and h) may occur very rapidly.
  3959: 
  3960:                                                                  61
  3961: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  3962: 
  3963: i) Device 0 sets the DRDY bit when ready to accept any command.
  3964: 
  3965:      NOTE 35 - Steps h) and i) may occur at the same time. While no maximum time is specified for the
  3966:      DRDY bit to become equal to 1 to occur, a host should allow up to 2 minutes for the DRDY bit to be
  3967:      set to 1. See figure 9.
  3968: 
  3969: 8.2.2 Software reset - device 1
  3970: 
  3971: a) Host sets SRST bit to 1 in the Device Control register;
  3972: b) Device 1 set the BSY bit no later than 400 ns after detecting that the SRST bit to equal to 1;
  3973: c) Device 1 negates PDIAG- no later than 1 ms after detecting that the SRST bit is 1;
  3974: d) Device 1 perform hardware initialization and diagnostics;
  3975: e) Device 1 may revert to its default condition;
  3976: f) Device 1 posts diagnostic results to the Error Register;
  3977: g) Device 1 waits for the host to set the SRST bit equal to 0;
  3978: h) Device 1 clears the BSY bit when ready to accept commands that do not require the DRDY bit to be equal
  3979: 
  3980:      to 1;
  3981: i) If Device 1 passed its diagnostics without error in step d), Device 1 asserts PDIAG-. If the diagnostics
  3982: 
  3983:      failed, Device 1 does not assert PDIAG- and continues to the next step. Device 1 shall clear the BSY bit,
  3984:      optionally assert PDIAG-, no later than 30 seconds from the time the host sets the SRST bit to 0. The
  3985:      device shall set the Sector Count register to 01h, the Sector Number register to 01h, the Cylinder Low
  3986:      register to 00h, the Cylinder High register to 00h, and the Device/Head register to 00h;
  3987: j) Device 1 sets the DRDY bit when ready to accept any command.
