  5082: 6) Post Device 1's initialization and diagnostic results:
  5083:     a) If Device 1 completed all initialization and diagnostic without error, Set the Error register to 01h and
  5084:     assert PDIAG-.
  5085:     b) If Device 1 failed any initialization or diagnostics, set the Error register to a value other than 01h (see
  5086:     Table 11) and do not assert PDIAG-.
  5087: 7) Set the status register to 00.
  5088: 
  5089:      NOTE 47 - Steps 2-7 complete within 30 s.
  5090: 
  5091: 8) Finish initialization and optionally finish spin up.
  5092: 9) Post Ready status:
  5093: 
  5094:     a) Set the DRDY bit to one and, if spin up is also complete, the DSC bit to one in the Status register.
  5095:     b) Negate DASP-.
  5096: 10) If not previously done, wait for spin up to complete and then set the DSC bit in the Status register to one.
  5097: 11) Negate DASP- when the Command register is written or after 30 s.
  5146: 6) Wait for SRST bit to be set to 0.
  5147: 7) Reset the Command Block registers:
  5148: 
  5149:     a) Set the Sector Count register to 01h.
  5150:     b) Set the Sector Number register to 01h.
  5151:     c) Set the Cylinder Low register to 00h.
  5152:     d) Set the Cylinder High register to 00h.
  5153:     e) Set the Device/Head register to 00h.
  5154: 8) Post Device 1's initialization and diagnostic results:
  5155: 
  5156:                                                                                                                                               81
  5157: X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  5158: 
  5159:     a) If Device 1 completed all initialization and diagnostics without error, set bits 6-0 of the Error register the
  5160:     value 01h and assert PDIAG-.
  5161:     b) If Device 1 failed any initialization or diagnostics, set bits 6-0 of the Error register to a value other than
  5162:     01h (see table 11) and does not assert PDIAG-.
  5163: 
  5164:      NOTE 51 - Steps 7-9 complete within 30 s.
  5165: 
  5166: 9) Set the DRDY bit in the Status register when ready to accept any command.
  5167: 
  5168: A.7 Diagnostic command algorithm

