   651: Introduction
   652: This standard is divided into the following clauses and annexes.
   653: This standard encompasses the following:
   654: Clause 1 describes the scope.
   655: Clause 2 lists the normative references.
   656: Clause 3 provides definitions, abbreviations, and conventions used within this document.
   657: Clause 4 contains the electrical and mechanical characteristics; covering the interface cabling requirements
   658: of the DC, data cables and connectors.
   659: Clause 5 contains the signal descriptions of the AT Attachment Interface.
   660: Clause 6 contains descriptions of the registers of the AT Attachment Interface.
   661: Clause 7 describes the general operating requirements of the AT Attachment Interface.
   662: Clause 8 contains descriptions of the commands of the AT Attachment Interface.
   663: Clause 9 contains an overview of the protocol of the AT Attachment Interface.
   664: Clause 10 contains the interface timing diagrams.
   665: Annexes A through E are informative.
   666: 
   667:                                                                                                                                                xi
   668: AMERICAN NATIONAL STANDARD                       X3.279-1996
   669: 
   670: American National Standard
   671: for Information Systems -
   672: 
   673: Information Technology -
   674: AT Attachment Interface with Extensions (ATA-2)
   675: 
   676: 1. Scope
   677: 
   678: This standard extends the AT Attachment Interface with the addition of new commands, and defines
   679: improved interface transfer rates. In addition, general improvements have been made in content for
   680: completeness and to improve clarity.
   681: 
   682: This standard defines the AT Attachment Interface and integrated interfaces between devices and host
   683: processors. It provides a common point of attachment for systems manufacturers, system integrators, and
   684: suppliers of intelligent devices.
   685: 
   686: The application environment for the AT Attachment Interface is any device which uses internal storage.
