  4423:                                              Figure 13 - DMA steps
  4424: 
  4425: 8.7 Device 0 only configurations
  4426: 
  4427: In a single device configuration where device 0 is the only device and the host selects device 1, device 0
  4428: may respond to accesses of the Command Block and Control Block registers in one of two methods. These
  4429: two methods exist because previous versions of the ASCI X3T10 standard did not specify the required
  4430: behavior for this configuration. The first method is the recommended implementation.
  4431: 
  4432: The first method is:
  4433:      a) A write to the Device Control register shall complete as if device 0 was the selected device;
  4434:      b) A write to the Command Block register, other than the Command register, shall complete as if device
  4435:      0 was selected;
  4436:      c) A write to the Command register is ignored;
  4437:      d) A read of the Control Block or Command Block registers, other than the Status or Alternate Status
  4438:      registers, shall complete as if device 0 was selected;
  4439:      e) A read of the Status or Alternate status register returns the value 00H.
  4440:      NOTE 41 - IDX is vendor specific and might change following reset or power mode changes resulting
  4441:      in other values for status other than 00H.
  4442: 
  4443: The second method requires that device 0 implement an Error, Status and Alternate Status register that is
  4444: used whenever device 1 is selected.
  4445: 
  4446: The second method is:
  4447:      a) The device 1 Error, Status and Alternate status registers are set to 00H by a reset;
  4448:      NOTE 42 - IDX is vendor specific and might change following reset or power mode changes resulting
  4449:      in other values for status other than 00H.
  4450:      b) A write to the Device Control register shall complete as if device 0 was the selected device;
  4451:      c) A write to the Command Block register, other than the Command register, shall complete as if device
  4452:      0 was selected;
  4453: 
  4454: 70
  4455:                                                                                                                X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  4456: 
  4457:      d) A write to the Command register with a command code other than the INITIALIZE DEVICE
  4458:      PARAMETERS or EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTICS command causes the device 1 Error, Status and
  4459:      Alternate status registers to be used as follows:
  4460: 
  4461:           1) the BSY bit is set in the device 1 status register;
  4462:           2) the ABRT bit is set in the device 1 Error register;
  4463:           3) the ERR bit is set in the device 1 status registers;
  4464:           4) the BSY bit is cleared in the device 1 status register;
  4465:           5) if the nIEN bit in the Device Control Register is cleared, the INTRQ signal is asserted;
  4466:           e) An EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command is executed as if it addressed to device 0;
  4467:      f) An INITIALIZE DEVICE PARAMETERS command is executed as if device 1 is present and is actually
  4468:      executing the command. The command shall have no effect of the device parameters of device 0;
  4469:      g) A read of the Control Block or Command Block registers, other than the Status or Alternate Status
  4470:      registers, shall complete as if device 0 was selected;
  4471:      h) A read of the Error, Status or Alternate status register returns the value in the device 1 copy of these
  4472:      registers. The device 1 status registers shall contain 00H following a reset and the value 01H following
  4473:      an attempt to execute a command, other than EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTICS or INITIALIZE
  4474:      DEVICE PARAMETERS, on device 1.
  4475: 
  4476: 9. Timing
  4477: 
  4478: 9.1 Deskewing
  4479: 
  4480: The host shall provide cable deskewing for all signals originating from the controller. The device shall
  4481: provide cable deskewing for all signals originating at the host.
  4482: 
  4483: All timing values and diagrams are shown and measured at the connector of either device connected to the
  5168: A.7 Diagnostic command algorithm
  5169: 
  5170: A.7.1 Algorithm for Device 0
  5171: 
  5172: 1) The EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command is received.
  5173: 2) The hardware should set 80h in the Status register within 400 ns.
  5174: 3) The hardware should set 80h in the Device 1* Status register.
  5175: 
  5176:      NOTE 52 - Steps 1-3 complete within 1 ms.
  5177: 
  5178: 4) Assert DASP-.
  5179: 5) Perform all the device diagnostics and note the results.
  5180: 6) Finish all the hardware initialization needed to get the device ready to receive any type of command from
  5181: the host including:
  5182: 
  5183:     a) Set the Sector Count register to 01h.
  5184:     b) Set the Sector Number register to 01h.
  5185:     c) Set the Cylinder Low register to 00h.
  5186:     d) Set the Cylinder High register to 00h.
  5187:     e) Set the Device/Head register to 00h.
  5188: 7) If Device 1 is present:
  5189:     a) Monitor PDIAG- until PDIAG- is asserted by Device 1 or for 6 s.
  5190:     b) If PDIAG- is asserted within 6 s, set bit 7 to 0 in the Error register.
  5191:     c) If PDIAG- is not asserted within 6 s, set bit 7 to 1 in the Error register.
  5192: 8) Post Device 0's initialization and diagnostic results:
  5193:     a) If Device 0 completed all initialization and diagnostics without error, set bits 6-0 of the Error register the
  5194:     value 0000001b.
  5195:     b) If Device 0 failed any initialization or diagnostics, set bits 6-0 of the Error register to a value other than
  5196:     0000001b (see Table 11).
  5197: 
  5198:      NOTE 53 - Steps 2-8 complete within 6 s.
  5199: 
  5200: 9) Set the Status register to 50h and set Drive 1* Status register to 00h.
  5201: 10) Assert INTRQ.
  5202: 
  5203: A.7.2 Algorithm for Device 1
  5204: 
  5205: 1) The EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC command is received.
  5206: 2) The hardware should set 80h in the Status register within 400 ns.
  5207: 3) Negate the PDIAG- signal.
  5208: 
  5209:      NOTE 54 - Steps 1-3 complete within 1 ms.
  5210: 
  5211: 82
  5212:                                                                                                                X3T10/0948D Revision 4c
  5213: 4) Assert DASP-.
  5214: 5) Perform all the device diagnostics and note the results.
  5215: 6) Finish all the hardware initialization needed to get the device ready to receive any type of command from
  5216: the host including:
  5217: 
  5218:     a) Set the Sector Count register to 01h.
  5219:     b) Set the Sector Number register to 01h.
  5220:     c) Set the Cylinder Low register to 00h.
  5221:     d) Set the Cylinder High register to 00h.
  5222:     e) Set the Device/Head register to 00h.
  5223: 7) Post Device 1's initialization and diagnostic results:
  5224:     a) If Device 1 completed all initialization and diagnostics without error, set bits 6-0 of the Error register the
  5225:     value 1 and assert PDIAG-.
  5226:     b) If Device 1 failed any initialization or diagnostics, set bits 6-0 of the Error register to a value of 2 or
  5227:     greater indicating the type of failure and do not assert PDIAG-.
  5228:      NOTE 55 - Steps 2-7 complete within 5 s.
  5229: 8) Set the DRDY bit in the Status register when ready to accept any command.
